### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- Track workouts, meals, and weight by just talking to your AI agent. Nexus is a remote MCP server that stores fitness data so you can log, query, and update your training and nutrition history conversationally.
- ## MCP Server
- Nexus is a remote MCP server. Connect via:
- https://nexus-tad5z6m6za-el.a.run.app/mcp
- Authentication is handled via OAuth 2.0 (Google sign-in through Supabase). The user will be prompted to authenticate on first use.
- ## Tools
- Nexus exposes 4 tools:
- ### `log`
- Store new workout and/or meal entries. Accepts:
- Always use `exercise_key` in lowercase_snake_case for consistency (e.g., `bench_press`, `pull_ups`). The server computes meal macro totals automatically.
- ### `history`
- Fetch entries with flexible querying:
- - Query by single date, date range, or last 7 days (default)
- - Filter by type: `workout`, `meal`, or `weight`
- - Access friend data via `friend_id` parameter
- - Returns `your_exercises` list for exercise name standardization
- - Returns `day_totals` when querying a single day
- ### `update`
- Modify existing entries by `entry_id` (obtained from `history`). Send the complete updated data object — the server recomputes meal totals after updates.
- ### `friends`
- Manage social fitness connections:
- - `list` — show current friends and pending requests
- - `add` — send a friend request using a friend code (format: `NEXUS-XXXX`)
- - `accept` / `reject` — respond to incoming requests
- - `remove` — remove an existing friend
- ## CLI
- Users can also install the Nexus CLI:
- Commands: `nexus auth`, `nexus log`, `nexus history`, `nexus update`, `nexus friends`
- - The server validates data shapes and returns clear error messages
- - Use the `your_exercises` list from `history` to keep exercise names consistent across workouts
